1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,729
This is Open Higgsfield Skills. One prompt in, a finished
video out, built entirely on open-weights Comfy workflows.

2
00:00:07,879 --> 00:00:12,660
It's agent-agnostic: thirty-five skills, and a video director
that any coding agent can drive.

3
00:00:13,509 --> 00:00:17,190
Every shot you're about to see was made by the pack, on a
single Google Colab GPU.

4
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:23,940
It starts with stills. FLUX Klein paints each keyframe, and a
judge scores it before a single frame of video gets rendered.

5
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:31,050
Approved stills come to life with LTX image-to-video: a fast
first pass, then a latent upscale for detail.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,509
Shots can chain. The last frame of one clip becomes the first
frame of the next, so the scene keeps moving without a jump.

7
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:45,100
Need a change? Qwen Image Edit rewrites a frame from one
sentence. The rain turns to snow, and the fox stays the same
fox.

8
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:49,410
BiRefNet cuts subjects out cleanly, ready for compositing.

9
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:56,090
And when you want an exact camera move, Wan Fun Camera takes a
name, like arc left, and flies it.

10
00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:04,400
On Google Colab, the runner skill packs everything into one
notebook: pinned ComfyUI, pinned nodes, the models, a spend
cap, and a watchdog that shuts the runtime down.

11
00:01:05,549 --> 00:01:11,170
The director keeps one resumable manifest of every prompt,
seed and model, so a dropped session picks up right where it
left off.

12
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:17,410
Voice, music, captions and the final cut are skills too. Even
this narration was generated by the pack.

13
00:01:18,359 --> 00:01:24,859
Open weights. Open skills. Open Source Higgsfield. Find it on
GitHub at mojomast/open-higgsfield-skills.

